). M013 monotonicity and M011 evaluate the enclosing interval's volume, giving ν(Jᵢ∩[0,1])≤ofReal(ρᵢ+ηᵢ). Hence the integral is at most ∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1)+∑'ᵢηᵢρᵢ^s≤∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1)+ε, because ηᵢρᵢ^s≤ε2^(−i−1) and these weights sum to 1. As ε>0 was arbitrary, C_s(E,δ)≤the cost of this fixed cover; if that cost is infinite this is immediate, and otherwise let ε decrease to zero. Since V was an arbitrary Nat-indexed δ-cover, taking the infimum over precisely this class of admissible covers yields C_s(E,δ)≤C_(s+1)(F,δ), not merely comparison with one selected cover. As δ decreases to zero the left side diverges, hence the right side diverges, so M008 gives H^(s+1)(F)=⊤. M014 implies s+1≤dim_H(F). Taking the supremum over all 0<s<D yields D+1≤dim_H(F).\"}]}}","status":"completed"}}

